  "summary_en": "Dutch ministerial regulation, effective 1 July 2019, setting application rules for permits to run experiments with self-driving vehicles without a driver on board, implementing the Experimenteerwet. It specifies required risk analyses, safety documentation, insurance, data recorders, remote supervision and cybersecurity measures, with the RDW handling applications.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Experiments with driverless vehicles (remote driver) require a permit; applications go to the RDW.",
   "Applicants must submit an action plan, functional description, risk analysis, and ISO 26262 and UN/ECE R10 evidence.",
   "Mandatory insurance in addition to WAM, and data recorder descriptions suitable for criminal proceedings.",
   "Descriptions of remote supervision, cybersecurity measures and passenger safety/evacuation protocols are required.",
   "Minister decides within six months; applicants must commit to knowledge sharing and monitoring."
  ],
